[Choose your path]($link.page('start')) and check
[Compatibility]($link.page('reference/compatibility')) for your hardware and model.

# [Build with ZML]($heading.id('build-with-zml'))

Use the inference framework to implement, compile, and run models in Zig.
Follow the [ZML quickstart]($link.page('zml/quickstart')) to build MNIST with
Bazel and classify a handwritten digit on CPU.

# [Serve models with LLMD]($heading.id('serve-models-with-llmd'))

Serve a checkpoint over HTTP. Follow the
[LLMD quickstart]($link.page('llmd/quickstart')) to start a server
and receive your first chat response. See [Operations]($link.page('operations'))
to deploy, monitor, and troubleshoot the service.
